\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {A3}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {The confounded ladder against the Mode-S instrument, on the CIFAR-10 arm that has both}; §\ref {app:sixcell} adds a CIFAR-100 arm that has both and reproduces the sign disagreement. Same downstream defense, same attack, same seeds, same nominal dose, and the two designs share their $\kappa {=}0$ cell \emph  {numerically} over all $20$ seeds (mean and worst per-seed gap $0.00\mathrm  {e}{+}00$, asserted at $10^{-12}$). \textbf  {Each row carries its own $n$, because this table is mixed.} A pre-registered top-up (\texttt  {experiments/\allowbreak  pre\_registration\_reversal\_seed\_topup.md}) added seeds $47$--$61$ to both legs at the two \emph  {endpoint} rungs, so the outcome rows are $n{=}20$; the mechanism rows are the frozen $n{=}5$ measurement on seeds $42$--$46$, which is the only $n$ they were ever recorded at. At the top rung the two designs are matched on aggregate displacement and decision change (at $n{=}5$) and on mean clean accuracy (at $n{=}20$), so \textbf  {the ladder's fall is not an accuracy collapse}; they differ chiefly in the \textbf  {adversarial coefficient channel}, and the ASR effect \textbf  {changes sign}. \textbf  {The one non-match, disclosed:} aggregate adversarial influence $\Lambda _a$ moves in \emph  {both} designs, $0.081$ against $0.033$ ($2.4\times $), so neither column is a clean statistic-only intervention, which is why the contrast is ``differ chiefly in the coefficient channel'', never ``only in it''. \emph  {Vocabulary:} this row is the $\Delta \Lambda _a$ column of the channel table (the adversarial share of selected coordinates, the same field in the same artifact) and \textbf  {not} its $\Delta $~adm.\ column, which counts rounds where the \emph  {support} of the adversarial mass changes and reads $0.000$ on every row: what moves here is how much weight the adversary's direction carries, not whether it enters at all. \textbf  {Which $p$ this is, since the top-up changed it.} Each effect's $p$ is the one-sided \emph  {endpoint} paired $t$ at that effect's own $n{=}20$, on the same per-seed differences as the interval beneath it. It is \emph  {not} the four-rung Jonckheere--Terpstra trend test: the interior rungs were not topped up, so that test stays at $n{=}5$ where it was frozen, and its values ($p_{\downarrow }{=}0.0015$, $p_{\uparrow }{=}0.069$, both $n{=}5$) are reported in §\ref {app:sixcell} rather than mixed into this column. This is a two-column contrast on one arm: it locates where the two designs differ, and attaches no $p$-value to the difference between the columns. Every cell recomputed from per-seed and per-round rows by \texttt  {build\_comparability\_table.py}, which also asserts that the published $n{=}5$ pair, $-0.272$ against $+0.098$, still reproduces on the frozen seed block; nothing here is retyped.}}{19}{table.caption.22}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:comparability}{{A3}{19}{\textbf {The confounded ladder against the Mode-S instrument, on the CIFAR-10 arm that has both}; §\ref {app:sixcell} adds a CIFAR-100 arm that has both and reproduces the sign disagreement. Same downstream defense, same attack, same seeds, same nominal dose, and the two designs share their $\kappa {=}0$ cell \emph {numerically} over all $20$ seeds (mean and worst per-seed gap $0.00\mathrm {e}{+}00$, asserted at $10^{-12}$). \textbf {Each row carries its own $n$, because this table is mixed.} A pre-registered top-up (\texttt {experiments/\allowbreak pre\_registration\_reversal\_seed\_topup.md}) added seeds $47$--$61$ to both legs at the two \emph {endpoint} rungs, so the outcome rows are $n{=}20$; the mechanism rows are the frozen $n{=}5$ measurement on seeds $42$--$46$, which is the only $n$ they were ever recorded at. At the top rung the two designs are matched on aggregate displacement and decision change (at $n{=}5$) and on mean clean accuracy (at $n{=}20$), so \textbf {the ladder's fall is not an accuracy collapse}; they differ chiefly in the \textbf {adversarial coefficient channel}, and the ASR effect \textbf {changes sign}. \textbf {The one non-match, disclosed:} aggregate adversarial influence $\Lambda _a$ moves in \emph {both} designs, $0.081$ against $0.033$ ($2.4\times $), so neither column is a clean statistic-only intervention, which is why the contrast is ``differ chiefly in the coefficient channel'', never ``only in it''. \emph {Vocabulary:} this row is the $\Delta \Lambda _a$ column of the channel table (the adversarial share of selected coordinates, the same field in the same artifact) and \textbf {not} its $\Delta $~adm.\ column, which counts rounds where the \emph {support} of the adversarial mass changes and reads $0.000$ on every row: what moves here is how much weight the adversary's direction carries, not whether it enters at all. \textbf {Which $p$ this is, since the top-up changed it.} Each effect's $p$ is the one-sided \emph {endpoint} paired $t$ at that effect's own $n{=}20$, on the same per-seed differences as the interval beneath it. It is \emph {not} the four-rung Jonckheere--Terpstra trend test: the interior rungs were not topped up, so that test stays at $n{=}5$ where it was frozen, and its values ($p_{\downarrow }{=}0.0015$, $p_{\uparrow }{=}0.069$, both $n{=}5$) are reported in §\ref {app:sixcell} rather than mixed into this column. This is a two-column contrast on one arm: it locates where the two designs differ, and attaches no $p$-value to the difference between the columns. Every cell recomputed from per-seed and per-round rows by \texttt {build\_comparability\_table.py}, which also asserts that the published $n{=}5$ pair, $-0.272$ against $+0.098$, still reproduces on the frozen seed block; nothing here is retyped}{table.caption.22}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {A1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {The criterion is a mechanism test, and the mechanism is measurable.} \textbf  {(a)} What C2 checks: the upstream transform $T$ and the statistic $S$ that $d_2$ reads determine an \emph  {invariance class} (Proposition~\ref {prop:invariance}), and the class determines the verdict: no composition needs to be run. This is why norm clipping does not blind FoolsGold but does blind Reputation. \textbf  {(b)} The measured chain for FG$\to $RFA, per round, on the transformed points RFA actually receives. Each marker is one round with $w_a>0$ (rounds where FoolsGold zeroes every adversary are Lemma~\ref {lem:annihilation} and carry no payload); large markers are mean~$\pm $~s.d. Corollary~\ref {cor:aggregate_mass}'s bound holds in every round, and the $\alpha {=}0.1$ collapse is visible as a collapse in the theorem's own quantity: $m$ falls from $4.71 \pm 1.51$ ($n{=}17$ rounds) to $2.06 \pm 2.35$ ($n{=}12$), with several rounds at $m{<}1$ where the bound degrades to $n_a/(n_b{+}n_a)$, and realized $\Lambda _a$ rises from $0.003$ to $0.085$ (max $0.50$) as composition ASR goes $0.093 \to 0.569$. Values below $10^{-4}$ are drawn at $10^{-4}$.}}{20}{figure.caption.23}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:mechanism}{{A1}{20}{\textbf {The criterion is a mechanism test, and the mechanism is measurable.} \textbf {(a)} What C2 checks: the upstream transform $T$ and the statistic $S$ that $d_2$ reads determine an \emph {invariance class} (Proposition~\ref {prop:invariance}), and the class determines the verdict: no composition needs to be run. This is why norm clipping does not blind FoolsGold but does blind Reputation. \textbf {(b)} The measured chain for FG$\to $RFA, per round, on the transformed points RFA actually receives. Each marker is one round with $w_a>0$ (rounds where FoolsGold zeroes every adversary are Lemma~\ref {lem:annihilation} and carry no payload); large markers are mean~$\pm $~s.d. Corollary~\ref {cor:aggregate_mass}'s bound holds in every round, and the $\alpha {=}0.1$ collapse is visible as a collapse in the theorem's own quantity: $m$ falls from $4.71 \pm 1.51$ ($n{=}17$ rounds) to $2.06 \pm 2.35$ ($n{=}12$), with several rounds at $m{<}1$ where the bound degrades to $n_a/(n_b{+}n_a)$, and realized $\Lambda _a$ rises from $0.003$ to $0.085$ (max $0.50$) as composition ASR goes $0.093 \to 0.569$. Values below $10^{-4}$ are drawn at $10^{-4}$}{figure.caption.23}{}}
