\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {A11}{\ignorespaces Mode~S (statistic-only), $n{=}5$ per arm ($n{=}8$ for \texttt  {cos\_krum}), per-attack mean ASR with the two measured channels. The decision channel moves far more than ASR throughout. \textbf  {The \emph  {admission} row is the admitted adversarial \emph  {mass} $\Lambda _a$}, i.e.\ Table~\ref {tab:channels}'s influence column $\Delta \Lambda _a$ and \emph  {not} its $\Delta $~adm.\ column, which records the support of that mass and is $0.000$ in every measured round of every arm; this section's hypothesis names (H-admission) are stated at the mass. $^{\dagger }$ below the $0.35$ accuracy gate. $^{\ddagger }$ the pre-registered replication arm, \emph  {rank-discordant} by design (smallest decision change, largest admission change of any interpretable arm) and scored against thresholds frozen separately at \texttt  {06d9bce} before \texttt  {results/dose\_replication/} existed: $\Delta {=}{+}0.098$ falls below reputation's $+0.178$, so the cross-arm admission \emph  {ordering} is refuted while the negative replicates on a different invariance class (below). Verdicts otherwise scored against the readings frozen at \texttt  {5130cec}; per-seed values in the supplement (§\ref {app:dose_detail}).}}{42}{table.caption.39}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:targeted}{{A11}{42}{Mode~S (statistic-only), $n{=}5$ per arm ($n{=}8$ for \texttt {cos\_krum}), per-attack mean ASR with the two measured channels. The decision channel moves far more than ASR throughout. \textbf {The \emph {admission} row is the admitted adversarial \emph {mass} $\Lambda _a$}, i.e.\ Table~\ref {tab:channels}'s influence column $\Delta \Lambda _a$ and \emph {not} its $\Delta $~adm.\ column, which records the support of that mass and is $0.000$ in every measured round of every arm; this section's hypothesis names (H-admission) are stated at the mass. $^{\dagger }$ below the $0.35$ accuracy gate. $^{\ddagger }$ the pre-registered replication arm, \emph {rank-discordant} by design (smallest decision change, largest admission change of any interpretable arm) and scored against thresholds frozen separately at \texttt {06d9bce} before \texttt {results/dose\_replication/} existed: $\Delta {=}{+}0.098$ falls below reputation's $+0.178$, so the cross-arm admission \emph {ordering} is refuted while the negative replicates on a different invariance class (below). Verdicts otherwise scored against the readings frozen at \texttt {5130cec}; per-seed values in the supplement (§\ref {app:dose_detail})}{table.caption.39}{}}
